I use meanness as an informal term to mean a bit more than just
the monster difficulty rating from 1 to 57.  I don't recall who I
picked
it up from over the years but I'm not the only poster who uses it like
that.

I tried using strength but that is a Nethack term so it ended up more
confusing.

I take meaness to be partially the difficulty rating used to determine
what monsters are generated at any one time.  I also include initial
equipment - The long sword damage makes the watch captain far
meaner than his difficulty rating.  I also include group size and
speed - soldier ant swarms are far meaner than the difficulty rating
that lets them get generated.  I also include special attacks - purple
worms are far meaner to non-player monsters with their instakill.

Just taking monster difficulty rating into account the difficulty of
monsters grows steadily with (XP + depth)/2.  Taking the other items
into account there are points where deaths spikes as it becomes
possible for out of depth monsters to be generated.


